  "title": "BNCI 2015-009 AMUSE (Auditory Multi-class Spatial ERP) dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 21 participants performing an offline auditory multi-class spatial oddball (P300) task for a brain-computer interface speller. Five frontal speakers with 45 degree spacing delivered unique 40 ms complex sounds under conditions varying in inter-stimulus interval (300 ms, 175 ms) and speaker configuration. Data comprise 60 EEG and 2 EOG channels, and were preprocessed and distributed through MOABB as BNCI 2015-009.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Brain Products amplifier using Ag/AgCl electrodes at 1000 Hz and nose reference, then bandpass filtered (0.1-250 Hz), downsampled to 100 Hz, and cleaned with threshold-based artifact rejection (>70 µV deflection over ocular channels). Participants mentally counted target stimuli, or responded by keypress in one condition. Target direction was cued visually and by a stimulus from that location before each block.",
